Wiring for elephance via the existing third-party mechanism, presence-conditionally.

STATUS: APPLIED to the tree on 2026-08-19 (verified: cargo check-all exit 0, elephance
compiled in the third-party collection). This file is regenerated from the live diff and
serves as the revert reference: git apply -R third-party/elephance/wire.patch

What it does:
- Root Cargo.toml: registers elephance in [workspace.metadata.third-party] (built as
  its own ephemeral workspace over twz/'s manifest, like kibi) and adds
  "third-party:elephance" to the initrd list.
- xtask build: a third-party entry whose local path is absent is skipped with a note
  naming the package and path, so trees without third-party/elephance/ build exactly
  as before — presence of this directory toggles elephance in and out.
- xtask image: searches all third-party compilations for an initrd crate instead of
  requiring every compilation to contain it (pre-existing bug that only bites with a
  second third-party package), and skips a third-party initrd entry only when its
  metadata path is genuinely absent (note names the path looked for) — a build that
  should have produced the binary still errors.

